1
00:00:07,913 --> 00:00:13,265
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,397 --> 00:00:15,428
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:23,419 --> 00:00:26,719
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:33,047
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:33,209 --> 00:00:37,698
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to benefit us all from these sessions

6
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:42,380
and to make us of those, who follow the best of words and apply them.

7
00:00:43,974 --> 00:00:46,974
Hanzhalah رضي الله عنه, one of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

8
00:00:47,831 --> 00:00:51,299
He got married right before the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

9
00:00:52,201 --> 00:00:59,305
And his first night with his wife was the night, right before the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

10
00:01:00,034 --> 00:01:05,928
Usually the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) should spend that time on base

11
00:01:06,847 --> 00:01:09,434
But Hanzhalah(حنظلة) sought permission from Rasool Allah ﷺ

12
00:01:09,482 --> 00:01:13,067
to allow him to go and spend that night with his wife.

13
00:01:14,177 --> 00:01:17,790
He is newly married, so he went to spend the night with the bride

14
00:01:18,511 --> 00:01:26,084
and early in the morning he goes and prays Fajr(فجر) with the Sahabah رضي الله عنه, with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

15
00:01:26,171 --> 00:01:28,036
 and then he goes back home.

16
00:01:28,878 --> 00:01:32,434
And his wife hold on to him

17
00:01:33,147 --> 00:01:35,823
and they sleep together

18
00:01:36,356 --> 00:01:42,799
and since it's getting late, he had to rush out and he did so without making Ghussl(غسل).

19
00:01:43,392 --> 00:01:47,212
He didn't take the shower, from the ritual impurity

20
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:53,773
and he goes to the battlefield, to fight the battle of Uhud(أحَد).

21
00:01:54,675 --> 00:01:59,584
And Hanzhalah رضي الله عنه, even though he was a foot soldier, he wasn't horseman,

22
00:02:00,353 --> 00:02:03,131
he attacked Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), who had a horse,

23
00:02:03,816 --> 00:02:06,063
so Hanzhalah(حنظلة) is attacking Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) on foot,

24
00:02:07,057 --> 00:02:10,333
which puts him to a disadvantage.

25
00:02:11,021 --> 00:02:20,862
But he tries and one of the enemy soldiers, strikes him with his spear

26
00:02:21,761 --> 00:02:27,320
and the spear hits him in the torso, and comes out from the other side.

27
00:02:28,262 --> 00:02:35,493
And Hanzhalah(حنظلة), not giving up try to pursue the enemy, who struck him.

28
00:02:36,416 --> 00:02:39,001
So, the enemy attacked him again and hit him another time

29
00:02:39,041 --> 00:02:44,507
and this time it was the fatal blow that killed Hanzhalah رضي الله عنه.

30
00:02:45,521 --> 00:02:49,861
After The battle was over, Rasool Allah ﷺ saw Hanzhalah(حنظلة),

31
00:02:49,974 --> 00:02:51,692
and he saw something strange.

32
00:02:52,634 --> 00:02:58,072
So, he told someone to go and ask his wife about him,

33
00:02:58,254 --> 00:02:59,182
 What happened.?

34
00:03:00,284 --> 00:03:03,850
So, they go and ask the wife of Hanzhalah(حنظلة), the wife of Hanzhalah(حنظلة) was Jamila(جميله),

35
00:03:04,259 --> 00:03:07,649
the daughter of the head of Al-Munafiqeen(منافقين), but she was a righteous woman.

36
00:03:08,566 --> 00:03:13,176
Jamila(جميله) and Abdullah(عبدالله) were both righteous children of Abdullah Bin Obaey(عبدالله بن ابيئ),

37
00:03:13,216 --> 00:03:15,173
 even though he was the head of Al-Munafiqeen(منافقين).

38
00:03:15,211 --> 00:03:18,348
And he also had a son who was good Muslim, his name was Abdullah(عبدالله).

39
00:03:19,379 --> 00:03:22,078
So, they go and ask Jamila(جميله), they said, What happened?

40
00:03:22,886 --> 00:03:28,065
So, she told them that I slept with my husband, and he didn't make Ghussl(غسل),

41
00:03:28,496 --> 00:03:31,350
and he left in the state of ritual impurity.

42
00:03:32,392 --> 00:03:34,374
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

43
00:03:34,966 --> 00:03:41,448
I saw Hanzhalah(حنظلة) right there, between the heaven and earth, being carried by the angels,

44
00:03:41,712 --> 00:03:46,705
and they were washing him with water from Paradise in vessels of silver.

45
00:03:47,932 --> 00:03:53,370
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله), the angels came down to wash Hanzhalah(حنظلة).

46
00:03:54,608 --> 00:03:59,815
And thus, he was called Ghaseel-Ul-Malaikah(غسيل الملائكه), the one washed by the angels.

47
00:04:01,955 --> 00:04:04,945
Another strange thing occurred, and that is,

48
00:04:05,175 --> 00:04:09,120
his wife after sleeping with her husband,

49
00:04:10,025 --> 00:04:16,573
calls in four witnesses to tell them that she has slept with Hanzhalah(حنظلة),

50
00:04:17,199 --> 00:04:19,487
which seems to be a very strange thing and it is,

51
00:04:19,527 --> 00:04:22,796
I mean, a husband sleeps with his wife.

52
00:04:23,271 --> 00:04:26,657
So, why go tell four people about it to be witnesses?

53
00:04:27,637 --> 00:04:31,189
So, they asked her, they said, I mean, why are you telling them, that this happened?

54
00:04:31,868 --> 00:04:33,656
She said, because I saw a dream,

55
00:04:34,656 --> 00:04:37,873
I saw that the sky opened, the heavens opened

56
00:04:38,708 --> 00:04:41,343
 and Hanzhalah(حنظلة) went through and then the sky closed.

57
00:04:41,831 --> 00:04:45,043
So I interpreted that dream to mean that Hanzhalah(حنظلة) would die as a Shaheed(شهيد).

58
00:04:46,308 --> 00:04:47,822
Now, why in the world,

59
00:04:48,507 --> 00:04:50,738
would a woman, who just got married,

60
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:55,614
want to sleep with her husband,

61
00:04:56,537 --> 00:04:59,262
and probably conceived from him,

62
00:05:00,184 --> 00:05:02,248
when she knows that he's gonna die the next day?

63
00:05:03,203 --> 00:05:04,105
Doesn't make sense.

64
00:05:04,145 --> 00:05:10,920
I mean, one would assume that the prudent thing to do, is to try to avoid conceiving from this man

65
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,056
 because he would be dead

66
00:05:12,446 --> 00:05:16,166
and that would make it easier for you to get married, after that,

67
00:05:16,605 --> 00:05:19,999
having no children and still a virgin woman.

68
00:05:21,155 --> 00:05:22,588
Why did you hold on to him?

69
00:05:22,628 --> 00:05:25,636
And then go on call four witnesses and tell them what happened?

70
00:05:26,508 --> 00:05:33,354
 You see, probably, it's difficult for us, to understand this.

71
00:05:33,394 --> 00:05:38,485
Because see, this shows you that the Sahabah(صحابه) had a different mindset than we did.

72
00:05:39,041 --> 00:05:41,739
They have a different worldview than we do.

73
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:46,081
They saw things differently, whether we're talking about political matters,

74
00:05:46,486 --> 00:05:48,318
and military matters,

75
00:05:48,731 --> 00:05:50,709
social matters, family matters.

76
00:05:51,379 --> 00:05:56,655
And this is something that it's sad that we see things differently and

77
00:05:57,063 --> 00:05:58,679
when we read about the lives of the Sahabah(صحاله),

78
00:05:58,719 --> 00:06:01,394
we kind of raised our eyebrows and say that this is strange.

79
00:06:02,451 --> 00:06:05,476
But to her this was the right thing to do.

80
00:06:05,955 --> 00:06:08,678
My husband is going to be a Shaheed(شهيد), I want to have a child for him.

81
00:06:10,236 --> 00:06:13,599
And I'm happy that my husband is gonna die as a Shaheed(شهيد).

82
00:06:13,639 --> 00:06:14,814
It's not that I'm sad.

83
00:06:14,854 --> 00:06:19,566
I mean, obviously, a wife wouldn't want her husband to leave her alone in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

84
00:06:20,001 --> 00:06:24,709
But it's for higher cause, it's for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

85
00:06:25,992 --> 00:06:28,389
And she was happy about it.

86
00:06:29,413 --> 00:06:31,933
You might wonder, who would marry her after having a child,

87
00:06:31,964 --> 00:06:32,718
No! Subhan Allah(سبحان الله),

88
00:06:32,775 --> 00:06:34,278
وَمَنْ يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَلْ لَهُ مَخْرَجًا

89
00:06:34,318 --> 00:06:36,273
If you have Taqwa(تقوى), Allah would find a way out for you.

90
00:06:36,394 --> 00:06:38,291
She ends up marrying Talha Bin Ubaid-Ellah(طلحه بن عبيدالله)

91
00:06:38,590 --> 00:06:40,710
one of the great Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

92
00:06:41,513 --> 00:06:46,624
By the way, she did have a son, a child from Hanzhalah(حنظلة) and his name was Abdullah(عبدالله).

93
00:06:47,007 --> 00:06:48,926
And this child was very proud.

94
00:06:48,974 --> 00:06:50,640
When people were asking, who are you?

95
00:06:50,683 --> 00:06:53,172
He would say I'm the son of the one, who was washed by the angels.

96
00:06:53,901 --> 00:06:55,712
Anyways, she got married to Talha(طلحه).

97
00:06:56,021 --> 00:07:04,527
And then Muhammad(محمد), her child from Talha(طلحه), was the one, who was the closest to Abdullah(عبدالله).

98
00:07:05,267 --> 00:07:10,124
And if Abdullah(عبدالله) would need anything, then it was his half brother Muhammad(محمد), who will take care of him.

99
00:07:10,166 --> 00:07:12,947
 So, even though Abdullah(عبدالله) would grow up as an orphan,

100
00:07:12,976 --> 00:07:16,750
but Allahعَزّوجَلّ has replaced what he would miss from his father,

101
00:07:17,033 --> 00:07:21,048
and he ended up getting it from his step father and from his half brother.

102
00:07:21,410 --> 00:07:25,860
So, if a person has Taqwa(تقوى), Allahعَزّوجَلّ will replace them with something, that is better.

103
00:07:26,845 --> 00:07:29,931
Allah will make up for you, what you have lost.

104
00:07:30,820 --> 00:07:36,522
Also, I want to point out here to you the level of obedience, that the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم had,

105
00:07:36,901 --> 00:07:38,866
here is a man who just got married

106
00:07:38,906 --> 00:07:44,474
 and early in the morning, the next day, he goes willfully to fight in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

107
00:07:44,815 --> 00:07:47,688
And he doesn't just go there to attend,

108
00:07:47,987 --> 00:07:49,908
 and to show that he was there,

109
00:07:50,239 --> 00:07:52,824
but in fact, pursues martyrdom,

110
00:07:53,284 --> 00:07:56,806
as we saw, in the case of attacking Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان),

111
00:07:57,243 --> 00:08:00,907
who was the leader of the army and definitely would be well protected.

112
00:08:01,514 --> 00:08:05,445
But he was searching for Shahadah(شهادة), even though I just got married last night.

113
00:08:06,074 --> 00:08:11,486
And I think that brothers, who have experienced marriage

114
00:08:12,103 --> 00:08:15,645
and can go back to the day that they got married,

115
00:08:16,107 --> 00:08:21,163
would realize how attached to Duniya(دنيا), they would be in those particular days.

116
00:08:21,650 --> 00:08:25,116
But the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم, they were connected to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

117
00:08:26,598 --> 00:08:28,638
We're carrying on with the stories of Shuhadah(شهدآء) from Uhud(أحَد).

118
00:08:28,677 --> 00:08:33,687
Abdullah Bin Amr Bin Haraam(عبدالله بن عمرو بن حرام) he told his son that,

119
00:08:34,334 --> 00:08:38,042
you are the dearest thing to me in this Duniyah(دنيا) after Rasool Allah ﷺ,

120
00:08:38,490 --> 00:08:41,153
and I would have wished you to die as a Shaheed(شهيد).

121
00:08:41,657 --> 00:08:45,197
But I want you to take care of your sisters and to pay my debt.

122
00:08:45,813 --> 00:08:48,879
And that's why his son stayed behind while he went to fight.

123
00:08:49,570 --> 00:08:52,828
And he was killed in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

124
00:08:53,428 --> 00:08:58,778
his son Jabir رضي الله عنه, and the family gathered around him and they were weeping,

125
00:08:59,150 --> 00:09:03,063
crying because of the loss of Abdullah Bin Haraam(عبدالله بن حرام).

126
00:09:03,602 --> 00:09:05,870
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them and this is in Bukhari(بخاري),

127
00:09:06,294 --> 00:09:12,374
whether or not you weep for him, the angels went on shading him with their wings,

128
00:09:12,934 --> 00:09:14,676
until you have lifted him up.

129
00:09:15,598 --> 00:09:17,807
Doesn't make a difference if you cry on him or not.

130
00:09:18,087 --> 00:09:24,030
He's happy and then Rasool Allah ﷺ meets Jabir(جابر) and it tells him,

131
00:09:24,166 --> 00:09:26,781
Shall I give you some glad tidings.

132
00:09:28,033 --> 00:09:29,519
Then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

133
00:09:29,919 --> 00:09:33,816
Allah greeted your father right there at Uhud(أحَد), where he was struck down.

134
00:09:34,661 --> 00:09:35,486
He then asked him.

135
00:09:35,858 --> 00:09:37,368
What is your wish Abdullah(عبدالله).?

136
00:09:37,796 --> 00:09:41,698
Allah u Akbar(الله اكبر), Allahعَزّوجَلّ is talking to His servants and calling him by his name.

137
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:43,327
What is your wish Abdullah(عبدالله)?

138
00:09:43,756 --> 00:09:45,574
What do you wish Me to do with you?

139
00:09:46,258 --> 00:09:47,942
So, Abdullah(عبدالله) replies,

140
00:09:48,030 --> 00:09:55,384
O Lord, to return me to the world, so that I may fight again for you and be killed once more.

141
00:09:56,288 --> 00:09:58,799
No one, absolutely no one,

142
00:09:59,406 --> 00:10:03,110
wants to go back to Duniyah(دنيا) except the Shaheed(شهيد).

143
00:10:04,290 --> 00:10:08,787
Everybody else would hate to go back to Duniyah(دنيا) and have to go through the agony of death one more time.

144
00:10:09,259 --> 00:10:11,741
But since the Shaheed(شهيد) doesn't taste that,

145
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:14,373
since the Shaheed(شهيد) doesn't suffer from that

146
00:10:14,664 --> 00:10:21,066
and only feels death, like a thorn or a sting of an insect.

147
00:10:21,636 --> 00:10:26,230
And after they see the great reward that Allahعَزّوجَلّ gives them, they wished to go back.

148
00:10:28,563 --> 00:10:32,265
So, these are some stories of the Shuhadaa(شهداء) of Uhud(أحَد).

149
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:35,259
Some of the virtues of Shuhadaa(شهدآء),

150
00:10:35,797 --> 00:10:38,734
some of the Ayaat(آيات) and Ahadith(احاديث) that were mentioned,

151
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:42,144
during the Battle of Uhud(أحَد), regarding the Shuhadah(شهدآء)

152
00:10:42,573 --> 00:10:47,028
and these Ayaat(آيات) and Ahadith(احاديث), even though they were said in the context of the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

153
00:10:47,108 --> 00:10:50,407
 but they apply to any Shaheed(شهيد) at anytime.

154
00:10:51,710 --> 00:10:52,586
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) said:

155
00:10:52,666 --> 00:10:56,935
The Prophet told me, when your brothers were struck down at Uhud(أحَد).

156
00:10:57,556 --> 00:11:00,910
Allah place their spirits in the crops of green birds

157
00:11:01,481 --> 00:11:05,081
that would go down to the rivers of Paradise and feed off the fruits there.

158
00:11:05,825 --> 00:11:11,031
Then they would retire to golden candelabra hung in the shade of the throne,

159
00:11:11,678 --> 00:11:14,662
enjoying their food, drink and lodging so well.

160
00:11:15,155 --> 00:11:18,337
They asked, Who can tell our brothers about us

161
00:11:18,905 --> 00:11:22,008
that we are alive in Paradise and being well provided for,

162
00:11:22,417 --> 00:11:26,916
so that they will not shirk Jihad(جهاد) and not be reluctant in warfare.

163
00:11:27,654 --> 00:11:30,104
So, they wanted somebody to go back and encourage their brothers

164
00:11:30,166 --> 00:11:32,610
and told them, carry on fight Fee Sabeel Lillah(في سبيل الله).

165
00:11:33,144 --> 00:11:36,637
And Don't be reluctant to join in, war.

166
00:11:37,259 --> 00:11:41,606
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ, the Almighty and glorious replied, I will inform them about you.

167
00:11:41,928 --> 00:11:44,052
And so Allah sent down in His book,

168
00:11:44,584 --> 00:11:48,357
verse 169, to 171, in Surat Al-Imran(سورةالعمران).

169
00:11:48,622 --> 00:11:55,331
وَلَا تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْوَاتًا ۚ

170
00:11:55,713 --> 00:12:00,358
بَلْ أَحْيَاءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ ۝

171
00:12:00,965 --> 00:12:06,519
فَرِحِينَ بِمَا آتَاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ

172
00:12:06,988 --> 00:12:12,926
وَيَسْتَبْشِرُونَ بِالَّذِينَ لَمْ يَلْحَقُوا بِهِمْ مِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ

173
00:12:13,265 --> 00:12:17,992
أَلَّا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا هُمْ يَحْزَنُونَ۝

174
00:12:18,267 --> 00:12:29,594
 يَسْتَبْشِرُونَ بِنِعْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَفَضْلٍ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُضِيعُ أَجْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

175
00:12:29,748 --> 00:12:33,886
And never think of those, who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead

176
00:12:34,470 --> 00:12:38,530
rather they are alive, with their Lord, receiving provisions,

177
00:12:38,972 --> 00:12:42,915
rejoicing, and what Allah has bestowed upon them, of His bounty.

178
00:12:43,290 --> 00:12:47,482
And they'll receive good tidings about those to be martyred after them,

179
00:12:47,951 --> 00:12:49,585
who have not yet joined them.

180
00:12:50,723 --> 00:12:53,226
That there will be no fear concerning them,

181
00:12:53,427 --> 00:12:54,802
nor will they grieve.

182
00:12:55,508 --> 00:12:59,219
They received good tidings of favor from Allah and bounty,

183
00:12:59,739 --> 00:13:04,112
and of the fact that Allah does not allow the reward of the believers to be lost.

184
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:06,738
So, number one, the Shaheed(شهيد) is alive.

185
00:13:07,296 --> 00:13:10,274
Number two, they want their brothers to carry on.

186
00:13:11,155 --> 00:13:14,626
And by the way, the bond of brotherhood that develops

187
00:13:15,064 --> 00:13:18,701
between the Mujahideen(مجاهدين) Fee Sabeel Lillah(في سبيل الله) is special.

188
00:13:19,565 --> 00:13:23,422
So, even after they die, they're still thinking about their comrades,

189
00:13:23,708 --> 00:13:26,640
their brothers in arms, the ones that were fighting with them,

190
00:13:27,065 --> 00:13:30,887
because of the special bond that develops among them.

191
00:13:31,311 --> 00:13:35,917
The Shuhadah(شهدآء) of Uhud(أحَد), were so eager to convey a message to their brothers,

192
00:13:35,981 --> 00:13:40,816
 who are still alive, that Allahعَزّوجَلّ offered to do that for them.

193
00:13:41,064 --> 00:13:46,295
And Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an were revealed, to convey that news to their brothers

194
00:13:46,621 --> 00:13:49,492
And these Ayaat(آيات) are still Ayaat(آيات) that we read today.

195
00:13:51,070 --> 00:13:55,058
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said, We asked the Messenger of Allah about this verse.

196
00:13:55,483 --> 00:14:01,737
And he replied their souls are in the crops of green birds that fly wherever they want.

197
00:14:02,470 --> 00:14:07,657
So, every one of them has a private jet to take them wherever they want in Jannah(جنه),

198
00:14:07,722 --> 00:14:10,418
they are the pilots and they can fly them wherever they want.

199
00:14:11,692 --> 00:14:16,291
Their souls are in the crops of green birds that fly wherever they want,

200
00:14:16,973 --> 00:14:21,067
then retire to candelabra, hanging near the throne.

201
00:14:21,583 --> 00:14:25,968
Once when they were there, your Lord looked over at them and said,

202
00:14:26,474 --> 00:14:28,001
ask whatever you want.

203
00:14:28,607 --> 00:14:32,124
They replied: What could we have to ask for

204
00:14:32,552 --> 00:14:34,927
flying about anywhere in paradise as we do?

205
00:14:34,969 --> 00:14:37,568
What do you want? I mean, What more can we ask for?

206
00:14:38,409 --> 00:14:41,178
So, Allah repeated His question to them three times.

207
00:14:41,695 --> 00:14:44,963
And when they realize that they would be asked again and again,

208
00:14:45,157 --> 00:14:50,669
They replied, we ask of you, that you return our souls to our bodies on Earth,

209
00:14:50,931 --> 00:14:54,318
so that we may be killed in your cause once more.

210
00:14:54,835 --> 00:14:59,530
And when Allah saw that this was the only request they would make, they were left alone.

211
00:15:00,261 --> 00:15:04,443
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) after insisting on them for three times, the only thing that could come up with.

212
00:15:04,754 --> 00:15:07,031
We want to go back and fight for Your sake.

213
00:15:08,423 --> 00:15:10,812
A story mentioned by Ibn Abi Duniyah(إبن ابي دنيا)

214
00:15:11,173 --> 00:15:13,292
narrated by Attaf Bin Khalid(عطاف بن خالد),

215
00:15:13,587 --> 00:15:15,635
he said that his Aunt related to him.

216
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:19,289
I rode one day to the graves of the martyrs,

217
00:15:19,711 --> 00:15:21,100
something she often did.

218
00:15:21,965 --> 00:15:25,420
And I stopped and prayed for a certain time near the grave of Hamza(حمزه).

219
00:15:26,657 --> 00:15:31,520
There was no one there in the valley except for the youth standing, holding the head of my mount.

220
00:15:32,019 --> 00:15:37,393
When I had finished I made the farewell gesture, indicating, Peace be upon you.

221
00:15:37,828 --> 00:15:40,733
Then I heard the greeting being returned to me,

222
00:15:41,358 --> 00:15:43,352
emanating from beneath the ground,

223
00:15:43,911 --> 00:15:49,065
I am as sure of this, as I am that a mighty and glorious Allah created me.

224
00:15:49,531 --> 00:15:53,929
And as I know night from day every hair of my body stood on end.

225
00:15:54,674 --> 00:15:57,810
So, they responded to her Salaam(سلام), they responded back to her Salaam(سلام).

226
00:15:58,720 --> 00:16:05,446
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that anyone, who goes and visits the grave of the Shuhadah(شهدآء) of Uhud(أحَد)

227
00:16:05,486 --> 00:16:08,827
 and gives them Salaam(سلام), they will respond back to it.

228
00:16:09,663 --> 00:16:14,502
Al-Waqidie(ألواقدي), he says: When Muawiyah(معاويه) was about to dig the canal.

229
00:16:15,189 --> 00:16:17,015
This is in the time of Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Muawiyah(معاويه),

230
00:16:17,055 --> 00:16:20,838
he wanted to dig a canal close to the cemetery of the Shuhadah(شهدآء) of Uhud(أحَد).

231
00:16:21,213 --> 00:16:25,314
He had the crier announced anyone who had relative killed at Uhud(أحَد), should be witness,

232
00:16:25,643 --> 00:16:28,669
because this canal might cut through some of the graves.

233
00:16:29,033 --> 00:16:31,881
He wanted the relatives of the diseased to be there,

234
00:16:32,112 --> 00:16:37,646
so that they would point out whose grave is it and move them as if necessary.

235
00:16:38,632 --> 00:16:42,393
Jabir رضي الله عنه said: A man came to me and said;

236
00:16:42,509 --> 00:16:47,864
Jabir(جابر), Some of Muawiyah(معاويه)'s workers have uncovered your father to site

237
00:16:48,282 --> 00:16:50,705
and part of him is outside the grave.

238
00:16:51,739 --> 00:16:54,673
So, Jabir(جابر) goes and he said, when we dug for them,

239
00:16:54,867 --> 00:17:00,214
I found my father in his grave lying as though asleep unchanged.

240
00:17:00,592 --> 00:17:04,415
We also found that his companion in the grave Amr Bin Jamooh(عمروبن جموح),

241
00:17:04,756 --> 00:17:10,206
had his hand over a wound and when it was removed, the wound emitted blood.

242
00:17:11,226 --> 00:17:16,038
It also says that the spade, struck the foot of Hamza(حمزه) and blood came out.

243
00:17:16,802 --> 00:17:22,378
Jabir رضي الله عنه said; We brought them out as though they had been buried the previous day.

244
00:17:22,763 --> 00:17:23,959
And Ibn Kathir(ابن كثير) said

245
00:17:24,274 --> 00:17:28,735
and it is said that the grave of each one of them may Allah be pleased with them

246
00:17:28,815 --> 00:17:31,238
 gave forth a scent like that of Musk.

247
00:17:31,549 --> 00:17:34,353
And how long after had they were burried, did this happen?

248
00:17:34,890 --> 00:17:36,945
46 years later,

249
00:17:37,573 --> 00:17:39,708
it was as if they were just buried

250
00:17:40,095 --> 00:17:43,656
and the smell of Musk was still coming out of their graves.

251
00:17:44,646 --> 00:17:46,982
These are Karamaat(كرامات) of the Shuhadaa(شهدآء).

252
00:17:48,835 --> 00:17:51,783
It is Sunnah(سنة) to bury the Shaheed(شهيد), where they die

253
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:54,374
 and not to move them to a different location.

254
00:17:54,696 --> 00:18:00,031
Because when some of the Sahabah(صحابه), were taking the dead bodies to Madina.

255
00:18:00,309 --> 00:18:04,153
Rasool Allah ﷺ said return them and have them buried at Uhud(أحَد).

256
00:18:04,683 --> 00:18:07,761
And that's where the cemetery of the Shuhadaa(شهدآء) is, it is in Uhud(أحَد),

257
00:18:08,042 --> 00:18:09,949
even though Madina was close by

258
00:18:10,259 --> 00:18:12,087
and they could have carried them to Madina,

259
00:18:12,315 --> 00:18:16,986
but Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted them to be buried in the sight of the battlefield.

260
00:18:17,283 --> 00:18:19,014
So, the scholars say that it's the Sunnah(سنة),

261
00:18:19,343 --> 00:18:22,111
to bury the Shuhadaa(شهدآء), where they die.

262
00:18:23,554 --> 00:18:26,620
Bukhari(بخاري) narrates, that Jabir رضي الله عنه said,

263
00:18:27,873 --> 00:18:35,696
the Messenger of Allah would place, one piece of clothing over each two of the men killed at Uhud(أحَد).

264
00:18:36,202 --> 00:18:40,184
And then would ask which one of these had a better knowledge of Qur'an,

265
00:18:40,643 --> 00:18:44,542
he would then place the one indicated in the grave first saying,

266
00:18:44,917 --> 00:18:47,096
I will testify for these at the Day of Judgment.

267
00:18:47,147 --> 00:18:49,701
So it shows you how poor they were

268
00:18:50,128 --> 00:18:57,025
they couldn't afford wrapping everyone in the necessary shroud, so they had to share.

269
00:18:57,497 --> 00:19:01,109
And also probably because of the exhaustion,

270
00:19:01,603 --> 00:19:04,369
they ended up burning more than one person in each grave.

271
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:08,645
And they would place the one who memorized more Qur'an first,

272
00:19:09,017 --> 00:19:10,893
and then they would place the second.

273
00:19:11,934 --> 00:19:15,909
Rasool Allah ﷺ ordered that they be buried in their blood,

274
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:18,060
he did not pray over them,

275
00:19:18,327 --> 00:19:19,633
nor were they washed

276
00:19:19,673 --> 00:19:21,123
and this is also in Bukhari(بخاري).

277
00:19:21,437 --> 00:19:25,319
So, this tells you the Sunnah(سنة), this is that the Shaheed(شهيد) is not washed

278
00:19:25,858 --> 00:19:29,036
and that there is no Salah(صلاة) of Janazah(جنازه) prayed for the Shaheed(شهيد),

279
00:19:29,122 --> 00:19:30,214
because he's not dead

280
00:19:30,469 --> 00:19:32,665
and the prayer of Janazah(جنازه) is for the dead.

281
00:19:33,027 --> 00:19:34,525
And since Shaheed(شهيد) is alive

282
00:19:34,895 --> 00:19:36,197
you don't pray Janazah(جنازه) on them.

283
00:19:36,617 --> 00:19:41,313
And also they be buried in their blood because Rasool Allah ﷺ says on the Day of Judgment,

284
00:19:41,615 --> 00:19:45,803
these injuries and this blood will be emitting the smell of musk.

285
00:19:46,281 --> 00:19:48,733
Rasool Allah ﷺ pray Salah-Tuz-Zuhur(صلاة الظهر)

286
00:19:49,669 --> 00:19:52,650
and as we said: Rasool Allah ﷺ was injured and exhausted.

287
00:19:53,478 --> 00:19:55,507
So, he had to pray sitting down.

288
00:19:56,548 --> 00:20:00,586
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ asked the Sahabah(صحابه) to line up because he's going to make Dua(دعا)

289
00:20:00,996 --> 00:20:03,332
and Rasool Allah ﷺ made this following Dua(دعا).

290
00:20:03,372 --> 00:20:05,182
And this is narrated by Imam Ahmad(إمام احمد),

291
00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:11,098
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: "O Allah to You is do all praise,

292
00:20:11,744 --> 00:20:15,677
O Allah, there is no grasping what You have dispersed,

293
00:20:16,114 --> 00:20:18,571
nor dispersing, what You grasped,

294
00:20:19,175 --> 00:20:23,338
there is no guiding aright, those whom You have led astray,

295
00:20:23,809 --> 00:20:27,880
nor any leading astray of those, You have guided,

296
00:20:28,506 --> 00:20:31,049
there is no giving of what You have prevented,

297
00:20:31,472 --> 00:20:34,403
nor any prevention of what You have given,

298
00:20:35,076 --> 00:20:39,025
there is no drawing close, what You have distanced,

299
00:20:39,443 --> 00:20:43,138
nor any distancing, what You have drawn close.

300
00:20:44,079 --> 00:20:51,400
O Allah, spread forth Your blessings, Your mercy, Your generosity and Your favors upon us.

301
00:20:52,149 --> 00:20:58,015
O Allah, I ask you those enduring blessings that never change nor seize,

302
00:20:58,548 --> 00:21:07,413
O Allah I asked you for blessings at time of the provation and security at time of fear.

303
00:21:07,938 --> 00:21:12,805
O Allah, I seek refuge with You against the evil of what You have given us,

304
00:21:13,137 --> 00:21:16,345
as well as from the evil from which You have saved us.

305
00:21:16,954 --> 00:21:22,081
O Allah have us view faith with favor and endear it to us well,

306
00:21:22,658 --> 00:21:27,172
have us view disbelief in morality and disobedience with antipathy.

307
00:21:28,214 --> 00:21:30,794
Place us among those who are well guided.

308
00:21:31,926 --> 00:21:35,076
O Allah take us to Yourself as Muslims,

309
00:21:35,548 --> 00:21:37,312
and give us life as Muslims

310
00:21:37,919 --> 00:21:39,544
Place us among the virtuous,

311
00:21:39,940 --> 00:21:42,119
not the shamed or the demented.

312
00:21:42,558 --> 00:21:45,651
O Allah, do battle with those disbelievers,

313
00:21:45,691 --> 00:21:49,060
who give the lie to your messengers, and who oppose them,

314
00:21:49,580 --> 00:21:51,083
torment and punish them.

315
00:21:51,456 --> 00:21:54,573
O Allah do battle against those disbelievers

316
00:21:54,626 --> 00:21:57,743
who are given the Scripture, Oh God of truth.

317
00:21:58,191 --> 00:22:01,984
This was the Dua(دعا) of Rasool Allah ﷺ after the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

318
00:22:03,423 --> 00:22:07,779
Ibn Is'haaq(إبن اسحاق) said: the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) took place on Saturday,

319
00:22:08,394 --> 00:22:09,675
in the middle of Shawwal(شوال).

320
00:22:10,409 --> 00:22:13,589
On the morning of Sunday, the 16th of Shawwal(شوال),

321
00:22:13,978 --> 00:22:17,128
the crier of the Messenger of Allah announced to the people

322
00:22:17,185 --> 00:22:19,552
that they should leave in pursuit of the enemy.

323
00:22:19,820 --> 00:22:22,515
Now the Muslims just came back from battle.

324
00:22:22,886 --> 00:22:25,857
They fought the battle on Saturday and Sunday morning

325
00:22:26,319 --> 00:22:29,674
the announcement is made that you have to pick up your arms

326
00:22:29,828 --> 00:22:32,210
get ready and pursue the enemy again.

327
00:22:33,710 --> 00:22:36,456
Now they are tired, exhausted, injured,

328
00:22:37,006 --> 00:22:39,732
they lost 70 of their men in one day.

329
00:22:40,339 --> 00:22:44,114
And now the next day immediately following the day of the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

330
00:22:44,531 --> 00:22:46,408
they're supposed to carry on a fight.

331
00:22:47,257 --> 00:22:50,613
So, this was very difficult to them, and the hypocrites didn't want to go out

332
00:22:50,653 --> 00:22:52,074
 and they made a big deal out of it.

333
00:22:52,114 --> 00:22:56,985
And they started spreading rumors because rumor came in that

334
00:22:57,297 --> 00:23:01,417
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) and his army are regrouping and planning another attack.

335
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:03,388
So hypocrites said, Are you crazy?

336
00:23:03,618 --> 00:23:05,729
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) has won yesterday.

337
00:23:06,041 --> 00:23:10,294
And now they're regrouping and they're receiving reinforcements.

338
00:23:10,552 --> 00:23:12,662
 And you want to go and fight them again.

339
00:23:14,093 --> 00:23:17,227
And these rumors were having their effect,

340
00:23:18,073 --> 00:23:20,975
but Rasool Allah ﷺ said, We'll go out and meet them.

341
00:23:21,923 --> 00:23:24,848
And Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق), reveals to us the purpose.

342
00:23:24,985 --> 00:23:30,606
He said, The purpose of the messenger of Allah in pursuing was to frighten the enemy.

343
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:34,531
This was by making them aware that they were still powerful,

344
00:23:34,595 --> 00:23:37,420
and that their losses had not so weaken them,

345
00:23:37,929 --> 00:23:40,042
that they could no longer face their enemy.

346
00:23:40,411 --> 00:23:42,433
Rasool Allah ﷺ is showing patience,

347
00:23:42,822 --> 00:23:46,052
he's showing steadfastness in face of danger,

348
00:23:46,596 --> 00:23:48,585
and he's showing persistence.

349
00:23:49,102 --> 00:23:55,180
And these are important qualities for the Muslims in their fight with the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

350
00:23:56,007 --> 00:23:59,119
Even if you're defeated, You carry on the fight.

351
00:23:59,637 --> 00:24:03,625
Even if your weakened you depend on Allahعَزّوجَلّ

352
00:24:04,198 --> 00:24:06,649
and you receive strength, from Him,

353
00:24:07,008 --> 00:24:09,844
and you remain steadfast and patient.

354
00:24:10,644 --> 00:24:15,693
I'll read to you what Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) said about the outcome of this battle.

355
00:24:16,468 --> 00:24:17,884
He said the Khuza'a(خزاعه) tribe,

356
00:24:18,287 --> 00:24:22,010
both those of them who were Muslims and those who were unbelievers

357
00:24:22,371 --> 00:24:26,266
were secretly the allies of Rasool Allah ﷺ in Tahamah(تهامه).

358
00:24:26,745 --> 00:24:32,297
And their understanding with him was that they would not conceal from him anything that happened there.

359
00:24:32,724 --> 00:24:35,361
So, these were tribes living in Tahamah(تهامه) in Hijaaz(حجاز).

360
00:24:35,756 --> 00:24:40,875
And whether the Muslims among them or the non Muslims, they were allies of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

361
00:24:41,191 --> 00:24:45,484
and they would bring him information about any movements that would occur in their area.

362
00:24:46,515 --> 00:24:50,138
Ma'bad(معبد) at that time was a Mushrik(مشرك), he was disbeliever.

363
00:24:50,579 --> 00:24:53,886
And he told Rasool Allah ﷺ, on his way past Hamra Al-Asad(حمراء ألأسد),

364
00:24:54,506 --> 00:24:58,177
Muhammad(محمد), we're deeply sorry at what happened to your men

365
00:24:58,700 --> 00:25:01,969
and we hope for Allah to protect you and them.

366
00:25:02,534 --> 00:25:06,220
So, even though it was a Mushrik(مشرك), but he was supportive of Rasool Allah ﷺ

367
00:25:06,269 --> 00:25:09,610
and he said, We wish that you would win against the people of Quraish(قريش).

368
00:25:09,766 --> 00:25:13,008
He then left while Rasool Allah ﷺ was still there at Hamra Al-Asad(حمراء ألأسد),

369
00:25:13,742 --> 00:25:15,776
and met up with Abu Sufiyan Bin Harb(ابو سفيان بن حرب)

370
00:25:16,165 --> 00:25:17,525
and his men at Raohaa(روحاء).

371
00:25:18,055 --> 00:25:21,605
They had decided to return to fight Rasool Allah ﷺ and his men.

372
00:25:21,787 --> 00:25:26,059
They had concluded we have severely damaged the best of his companions,

373
00:25:26,527 --> 00:25:28,425
and their chieftains and nobles.

374
00:25:28,936 --> 00:25:33,297
So, should we now go home before we uproot them completely,

375
00:25:33,509 --> 00:25:37,426
we should go back for the rest of them and be finished with them.

376
00:25:37,573 --> 00:25:39,302
 So this was the plan of the Kuffar(كفار).

377
00:25:40,122 --> 00:25:42,563
When Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) saw Ma'bad(معبد) he asked him,

378
00:25:42,958 --> 00:25:45,079
How are things back up behind you Ma'bad(معبد),

379
00:25:45,607 --> 00:25:48,358
he replied; Muhammad(محمد) has come out with his men

380
00:25:48,668 --> 00:25:52,475
seeking you in a force the likes of which I never saw before.

381
00:25:52,515 --> 00:25:53,552
And this wasn't true.

382
00:25:53,970 --> 00:25:56,666
But Ma'bad(معبد) is exaggerating the strength of the Muslims.

383
00:25:57,154 --> 00:25:59,795
They are truly in rage towards you,

384
00:26:00,147 --> 00:26:04,341
he has been joined by those who stayed behind when you did battle with him.

385
00:26:04,722 --> 00:26:07,606
And these men much regret what they did?

386
00:26:07,951 --> 00:26:12,403
The anger they have towards you is something the like of which I've never seen before.

387
00:26:13,503 --> 00:26:15,694
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said; What are you suggesting?

388
00:26:16,246 --> 00:26:20,071
He replied, I swear, I don't think you'll be able to leave

389
00:26:20,311 --> 00:26:23,002
 before you catch sight of the forelocks of their cavalry,

390
00:26:23,042 --> 00:26:24,604
 meaning they're coming fast.

391
00:26:25,505 --> 00:26:29,124
But we've decided to attack them to destroy the rest of them.

392
00:26:29,288 --> 00:26:30,810
That was the response of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان).

393
00:26:30,850 --> 00:26:31,733
Ma'bad(معبد) said;

394
00:26:31,938 --> 00:26:35,066
I really do advise you against that I swear.

395
00:26:35,575 --> 00:26:39,565
I was so affected by what I saw that I can post some verses on the subject.

396
00:26:40,029 --> 00:26:43,723
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said, What did you compose, Ma'bad(معبد) recited the verses he said,

397
00:26:44,628 --> 00:26:48,343
At the noise my mount almost shied....

398
00:26:48,897 --> 00:26:51,625
The earth streaming with masses of fine horses....

399
00:26:52,294 --> 00:26:55,491
Racing on their riders like noble lions....

400
00:26:55,899 --> 00:26:59,641
men, not effeminate in the fray and not poorly armed....

401
00:27:00,253 --> 00:27:03,386
I ran on thinking the earth itself moving....

402
00:27:03,816 --> 00:27:06,914
as they brought up a leader never to be forsaken....

403
00:27:07,486 --> 00:27:09,724
And I said, Woe to Ibn Harb(ابن حرب)....

404
00:27:10,152 --> 00:27:13,749
When you meet the plane shakes beneath the lions of men....

405
00:27:14,277 --> 00:27:16,527
I warn the people of Makkah very plainly....

406
00:27:16,964 --> 00:27:20,135
Addressing every wise insane man they have....

407
00:27:20,931 --> 00:27:24,000
Of the army of Ahmad(احمد) not some mixed rebel....

408
00:27:24,486 --> 00:27:28,856
And my warning should not be described as mere hearsay....

409
00:27:29,533 --> 00:27:35,149
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), when he heard this his party were dissuaded and they went back.

410
00:27:35,269 --> 00:27:40,646
 So, Ma'bad(معبد) did very well job in demoralizing the enemy and sending them back

411
00:27:41,073 --> 00:27:46,685
by convincing them that they have no chance of winning against Rasool Allah ﷺ and his Sahabah(صحابه).

412
00:27:46,995 --> 00:27:48,665
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed Ayaat(آيات)

413
00:27:49,257 --> 00:27:50,487
talking about this incident,

414
00:27:50,551 --> 00:27:54,138
the Munafiqeen(منافقين) saying that the Muslims should not go out and fight

415
00:27:54,488 --> 00:27:57,824
and the confidence that the Muslims had in victory,

416
00:27:58,153 --> 00:28:01,577
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says and these are verses 172 to 175.

417
00:28:01,819 --> 00:28:10,101
الَّذِينَ اسْتَجَابُوا لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا أَصَابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ ۚ

418
00:28:10,285 --> 00:28:16,274
لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا مِنْهُمْ وَاتَّقَوْا أَجْرٌعَظِيمٌ۝

419
00:28:16,672 --> 00:28:25,044
الَّذِينَ قَالَ لَهُمُ النَّاسُ إِنَّ النَّاسَ قَدْ جَمَعُوا لَكُمْ فَاخْشَوْهُمْ

420
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:28,909
فَاخْشَوْهُمْ فَزَادَهُمْ إِيمَانًا

421
00:28:29,119 --> 00:28:33,886
 وَقَالُوا حَسْبُنَا اللَّهُ وَنِعْمَ الْوَكِيلُ۝

422
00:28:34,205 --> 00:28:42,720
فَانْقَلَبُوا بِنِعْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَفَضْلٍ لَمْ يَمْسَسْهُمْ سُوءٌ

423
00:28:43,024 --> 00:28:52,033
 لَمْ يَمْسَسْهُمْ سُوءٌ وَاتَّبَعُوا رِضْوَانَ اللَّهِ ۗ وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَظِيمٍ۝

424
00:28:52,551 --> 00:28:59,559
إِنَّمَا ذَٰلِكُمُ الشَّيْطَانُ يُخَوِّفُ أَوْلِيَاءَهُ

425
00:28:59,841 --> 00:29:06,698
فَلَا تَخَافُوهُمْ وَخَافُونِ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُؤْمِنِينَ۝

426
00:29:07,097 --> 00:29:11,768
Those believers, who responded to Allah and the messenger

427
00:29:12,225 --> 00:29:14,084
after injury had struck them.

428
00:29:14,643 --> 00:29:18,280
For those who did good among them and feared Allah, is a great reward.

429
00:29:19,275 --> 00:29:22,419
Those to whom the people, i.e. the hypocrites said,

430
00:29:22,906 --> 00:29:26,119
Indeed the people have gathered against you, so fear them.

431
00:29:27,085 --> 00:29:29,885
But it merely increased them in faith.

432
00:29:29,925 --> 00:29:35,275
And they said sufficient for us is Allah, and He is the best disposer of affairs.

433
00:29:36,264 --> 00:29:38,536
So, the true believers in front of these rumors,

434
00:29:39,225 --> 00:29:43,305
which were by Shaytan(شيطان) and the hypocrites with the intention of weakening their morale.

435
00:29:43,862 --> 00:29:45,762
These rumors made them stronger.

436
00:29:46,420 --> 00:29:46,885
And they said;

437
00:29:46,925 --> 00:29:48,739
حسبنا الله ونعمل وكيل,

438
00:29:49,206 --> 00:29:53,525
sufficient for us is Allah and He is the best disposer of affairs.

439
00:29:53,960 --> 00:29:55,047
And then Allah says;

440
00:29:55,214 --> 00:29:59,961
So they returned with favor from Allah and bounty, no harm, haven't touched them.

441
00:30:00,001 --> 00:30:00,976
They didn't even fight

442
00:30:01,390 --> 00:30:03,620
and they pursued the pleasure of Allah.

443
00:30:03,982 --> 00:30:07,735
So, they didn't fight, but they still received the pleasure of Allah

444
00:30:08,357 --> 00:30:10,912
and Allah is the possessor of great bounty,

445
00:30:11,354 --> 00:30:15,351
that is only Satan who frightens you of his supporters

446
00:30:15,801 --> 00:30:19,815
so fear them not but fear Me, if you are indeed believers.

447
00:30:20,725 --> 00:30:23,235
So, Shaytan(شيطان) would come to us and say that

448
00:30:23,300 --> 00:30:25,464
the enemy is powerful, the enemy is strong,

449
00:30:25,504 --> 00:30:29,953
 look at his aircraft, look at his tanks, look at his rockets,

450
00:30:29,993 --> 00:30:32,669
look at his weapons, look at the numbers of his army

451
00:30:32,997 --> 00:30:37,646
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ says that, it is just from Shaytan(شيطان), with the purpose of weakening you.

452
00:30:37,994 --> 00:30:38,631
But if you say;

453
00:30:38,671 --> 00:30:40,687
حسبي الله ونعمل وكيل

454
00:30:40,882 --> 00:30:43,524
and if you depend on Allahعَزّوجَلّ, Allah will give you victory.

455
00:30:44,607 --> 00:30:49,297
The only prisoner of war that was taken by the Muslims in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

456
00:30:50,024 --> 00:30:51,609
ironically was Abu Azza(ابو عزى).

457
00:30:52,265 --> 00:30:53,679
You remember Abu Azza(ابو عزى),

458
00:30:53,888 --> 00:30:58,805
Abu Azza(ابو عزى) was the one, who was captured by the Muslims in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

459
00:30:58,845 --> 00:31:03,130
and he told Rasool Allah ﷺ that I am poor, and I have daughters.

460
00:31:03,823 --> 00:31:05,134
So, set me free

461
00:31:05,174 --> 00:31:08,248
and Rasool Allah ﷺ set him free, without paying any ransom.

462
00:31:08,359 --> 00:31:14,931
And he took from him an oath that he would never support an enemy against Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Azza(ابو عزى) agreed.

463
00:31:15,934 --> 00:31:17,626
But when he goes back to Makkah,

464
00:31:18,194 --> 00:31:22,165
and it's time for the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) to leave for the battle of Uhud(أحَد),

465
00:31:22,733 --> 00:31:26,171
they tell them to join he said no, I've given my word to Muhammadﷺ

466
00:31:26,211 --> 00:31:27,532
 that I'm not gonna fight against him.

467
00:31:27,804 --> 00:31:31,710
So, they kept on trying to convince him, until they fooled him and deceived him

468
00:31:32,023 --> 00:31:33,525
and he did join the army

469
00:31:33,565 --> 00:31:39,114
and Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) he ended up as the only one taken as a prisoner of war and this is an Aayah(آية) from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

470
00:31:39,584 --> 00:31:44,111
Now, he again tries to play the same trick against Rasool Allah ﷺ

471
00:31:44,151 --> 00:31:49,442
by saying that my daughters are in need, I'm a poor man, so set me free.

472
00:31:49,887 --> 00:31:51,476
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him,

473
00:31:52,138 --> 00:31:57,677
I will not let you stroke your beard and say that you have deceived Muhammad(محمد) twice

474
00:31:58,537 --> 00:31:59,907
and he ordered him to be beheaded.

475
00:31:59,947 --> 00:32:05,340
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said, believer will not be bitten twice from the same layer.

476
00:32:06,041 --> 00:32:09,441
So, Muslims should not be fooled, a Muslim should not be tricked

477
00:32:09,908 --> 00:32:11,728
and a Muslim should not be naive.

478
00:32:12,962 --> 00:32:18,622
Give some examples of the good ending and the evil ending because the end is what counts.

479
00:32:19,331 --> 00:32:22,431
Your last moments on this world are very important.

480
00:32:23,429 --> 00:32:29,032
Because your faith depends on your ending in this Duniyah(دنيا).

481
00:32:30,091 --> 00:32:36,309
We have in battle of Uhud(أحَد), examples of good ending and an evil ending.

482
00:32:37,194 --> 00:32:41,203
Kazmaan(كزمان) for example, one of the men from Madina,

483
00:32:42,298 --> 00:32:44,065
he wasn't interested in Islam.

484
00:32:45,022 --> 00:32:48,328
But when the Muslims went out to fight in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد), he joined them,

485
00:32:48,796 --> 00:32:52,900
and whenever the name of Kazmaan(كزمان) would be mentioned in front of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

486
00:32:52,916 --> 00:32:53,740
he would say;

487
00:32:53,764 --> 00:32:54,630
 اِنَّه’ فِيْ النَّارْ

488
00:32:54,670 --> 00:32:55,876
He is in hellfire

489
00:32:56,557 --> 00:32:59,565
But the Sahabah(صحابه) saw that he was fighting like a lion,

490
00:32:59,836 --> 00:33:07,636
and he has killed at least seven disbelievers before he fell due to his wounds.

491
00:33:08,476 --> 00:33:10,744
So, this made some of them skeptical.

492
00:33:10,784 --> 00:33:16,603
I mean, how could this man go to Hellfire when he has fought so hard?

493
00:33:17,346 --> 00:33:19,428
But then they came to him.

494
00:33:20,079 --> 00:33:23,152
Some of the Sahabah(صحابه) came to him and said;

495
00:33:23,341 --> 00:33:28,823
Some of his people from Madina came to him and said; Congratulations for being a martyr

496
00:33:29,533 --> 00:33:30,581
for being a Shaheed(شهيد).

497
00:33:31,351 --> 00:33:34,362
He said, Why are you congratulating me for Shahadah(شهادة).

498
00:33:34,924 --> 00:33:38,600
I didn't fight for the sake of Islam, I fought for the sake of my people.

499
00:33:39,365 --> 00:33:42,331
So, this man is fighting with the wrong intentions

500
00:33:42,918 --> 00:33:44,281
and then he dies.

501
00:33:44,908 --> 00:33:47,116
And he goes to hell fire

502
00:33:47,831 --> 00:33:53,352
because he didn't fight Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله), he didn't fight for the intention of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

503
00:33:54,238 --> 00:33:56,738
So, this is an example of the evil ending

504
00:33:57,222 --> 00:33:59,231
Mukhaireeq(مخيريق) was a Jew.

505
00:33:59,725 --> 00:34:01,491
He goes to his people and tells them:

506
00:34:01,571 --> 00:34:04,263
O Jews, You have learned,

507
00:34:04,303 --> 00:34:08,795
I swear by Allah, that it is your duty to help Muhammad(محمد) to victory.

508
00:34:09,394 --> 00:34:11,692
They said this is the Sabbath(سابت) we're not gonna fight.

509
00:34:12,097 --> 00:34:13,906
So, he left them and he said;

510
00:34:14,184 --> 00:34:19,785
If I should fall then my wealth goes to Muhammad(محمد) to do with it as he wishes.

511
00:34:20,514 --> 00:34:23,630
So, not only does he joined the Muslims in fighting,

512
00:34:23,951 --> 00:34:31,108
but he also makes his will that his inheritance is taken by Muhammadﷺ to spend as he wishes.

513
00:34:31,916 --> 00:34:35,360
Mukhaireeq(مخيريق) was killed, Rasool Allah ﷺ then said;

514
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:37,670
 مُخَيْرِيْقْ خَيْرُ يَهُوْدْ

515
00:34:37,965 --> 00:34:40,699
Mukhaireeq(مخيريق) is the very best of Jews.

516
00:34:41,364 --> 00:34:42,520
And the Sohaili(سهيلي) said;

517
00:34:42,846 --> 00:34:48,695
The message of Allah converted Mukhaireeq(مخيريق) property consisting of seven orchards into a Waqf(وقف),

518
00:34:49,150 --> 00:34:51,680
charitable endowment in Madina

519
00:34:52,021 --> 00:34:57,491
and Muhammad Ibn Ka'ab Al-Quraidhi(محمد ابن كعب القرظي) said; This was Madina's very first Waqf(وقف).

520
00:34:57,971 --> 00:35:01,750
The first endowment in Madina was that of the Jew, Mukhaireeq(مخيريق).

521
00:35:02,198 --> 00:35:07,078
Now there's a difference of opinion between scholars of whether he embraced Islam or died as a Jew.

522
00:35:07,446 --> 00:35:11,454
With the majority of them saying that he did actually embraced Islam.

523
00:35:12,069 --> 00:35:15,399
And when Rasool Allah ﷺ said that he's the best of Jews.

524
00:35:15,730 --> 00:35:19,017
That means Jews as an ethnicity and not a religion.

525
00:35:19,445 --> 00:35:21,336
So, he's the best of the Jewish people,

526
00:35:21,903 --> 00:35:23,775
but he is a Muslim in faith.

527
00:35:24,582 --> 00:35:27,231
So, that's an example of a good ending.

528
00:35:28,321 --> 00:35:29,695
And then there's Usairym(أصيرم),

529
00:35:30,080 --> 00:35:33,643
who was from Al-Aos(ألاوس), but he wasn't interested in Islam.

530
00:35:33,683 --> 00:35:34,778
He was a Mushrik(مشرك).

531
00:35:35,399 --> 00:35:37,107
He didn't embrace Islam yet.

532
00:35:38,086 --> 00:35:41,783
And when the Muslims left for the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

533
00:35:41,842 --> 00:35:43,396
He said, where is Sa'ad Ibn Muadh(سعد ابن معاد),

534
00:35:43,436 --> 00:35:44,316
 they said, he is at Uhud(أحَد),

535
00:35:44,354 --> 00:35:45,246
Where is so and so,

536
00:35:45,275 --> 00:35:45,656
He's at Uhud(أحَد).

537
00:35:45,680 --> 00:35:47,068
Where is so and so, they said, He's at Uhud(أحَد).

538
00:35:47,257 --> 00:35:49,780
So, he said that if all of my people are fighting in Uhud(أحَد), I am going to join them.

539
00:35:50,427 --> 00:35:53,839
And he did join with the Muslims in Uhud(أحَد) and he fought

540
00:35:54,385 --> 00:35:55,863
and he was wounded.

541
00:35:56,808 --> 00:35:58,860
So, before he dies,

542
00:35:59,506 --> 00:36:01,422
some of his relatives come to him and said,

543
00:36:01,976 --> 00:36:03,877
when they saw him, they said; This is Usairym(أصيرم),

544
00:36:04,427 --> 00:36:06,790
as far as we know, he wasn't interested in becoming Muslim.

545
00:36:06,830 --> 00:36:07,947
What is he doing here?

546
00:36:08,197 --> 00:36:10,652
So, they rush up to him and they asked them they asked him, Usairym(أصيرم),

547
00:36:10,957 --> 00:36:14,092
did you fight for the sake of Islam?

548
00:36:14,548 --> 00:36:16,525
Or did you fight for the honor of your people?

549
00:36:16,565 --> 00:36:17,558
He said, No

550
00:36:17,598 --> 00:36:20,107
I fought for the sake of Islam.

551
00:36:20,496 --> 00:36:23,083
So, Usairym(أصيرم) is the opposite of Kazmaan(كزمان).

552
00:36:23,579 --> 00:36:24,729
And then he dies.

553
00:36:25,540 --> 00:36:27,528
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said, he is in Jannah(جنة).

554
00:36:28,137 --> 00:36:30,266
Abu Hurairah(ابو هريره) would later on, ask the people,

555
00:36:30,613 --> 00:36:32,034
he would quiz them, he would say,

556
00:36:32,314 --> 00:36:38,820
Tell me about a man, who entered into Jannah(جنة) without praying one prayer to Allahعَزّوجَلّ

557
00:36:39,333 --> 00:36:41,844
and if they don't know, the answer, he'd tell them, it was Usairym(أصيرم).

558
00:36:42,126 --> 00:36:43,972
Rasool Allah ﷺ said in Bukhari(بخاريْ),

559
00:36:44,668 --> 00:36:47,589
عَمَلًا يَسِيْرًا وَاَجْرًا كَثِيْرًا

560
00:36:47,999 --> 00:36:51,012
He did very little but he was rewarded a lot.

561
00:36:51,647 --> 00:36:54,064
Therefore Shahadah(شهادة) is the one deed

562
00:36:54,750 --> 00:36:57,964
that would guarantee a person the highest levels of Jannah(جنة)

563
00:36:58,273 --> 00:37:00,032
without doing anything else.

564
00:37:00,871 --> 00:37:04,732
Here Usairym(أصيرم) didn't prayed, did not fast, did not do anything.

565
00:37:05,446 --> 00:37:06,574
All what he did was, say

566
00:37:06,598 --> 00:37:08,850
اَشْهَدُ الله اله الا الله وَ اشْهَدُاَنَّ محمد الرَسُول الله

567
00:37:08,890 --> 00:37:10,094
and then he died as a Shaheed(شهيد)

568
00:37:10,362 --> 00:37:13,735
and receives the high levels of Jannah(جنة), great reward.

569
00:37:14,480 --> 00:37:16,831
Some miracles that occurred in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

570
00:37:17,398 --> 00:37:21,800
Number one, the eye of Qatadah(قتاده), if I mentioned this as miracle in the Battle of Badr(بدر)

571
00:37:21,880 --> 00:37:24,663
 but it is mentioned as miracle in Badr(بدر) and Uhud(أحَد),

572
00:37:25,099 --> 00:37:28,386
there is a difference of opinion among the scholars on where it happened.

573
00:37:29,263 --> 00:37:32,354
Some of them say that it occurred in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

574
00:37:32,529 --> 00:37:37,219
So, we can attribute that to the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) as one of the miracles of the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

575
00:37:37,259 --> 00:37:42,379
Another one is what happened with Obaey Bin Khalaf(أبي بن خلف), one of the leaders of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

576
00:37:42,481 --> 00:37:46,305
one of the Mushriqeen(مشركين), one of the worst enemies of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

577
00:37:47,244 --> 00:37:51,210
Obaey Bin Khalaf(أبي بن خلف), he used to say I'm going to kill Muhammad(محمد).

578
00:37:52,021 --> 00:37:53,078
I'm going to kill Muhammad(محمد)

579
00:37:53,626 --> 00:37:55,544
when that news reached to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

580
00:37:55,584 --> 00:37:58,448
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No, I will kill him.

581
00:37:59,169 --> 00:38:01,758
So, in the Battle of Uhud, Obaey Bin Khalaf(أبيئ بن خلف)

582
00:38:02,289 --> 00:38:05,350
charges at Muhammadﷺ on his horse

583
00:38:06,057 --> 00:38:10,626
and he used to feed this horse special food, he used to feed this horse corn

584
00:38:11,170 --> 00:38:15,261
and special food and he would say I'm going to kill Muhammad(محمد) on you.

585
00:38:15,954 --> 00:38:19,155
So, he charges at Muhammadﷺ and the Sahabah(صحابه) say,

586
00:38:19,447 --> 00:38:24,954
they want to volunteer and stop his attack at the Messenger of Allah,

587
00:38:25,010 --> 00:38:26,280
but Rasool Allah didn't allow them.

588
00:38:26,320 --> 00:38:28,164
He said; No, leave him.

589
00:38:28,735 --> 00:38:31,042
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ picks up a spear

590
00:38:31,302 --> 00:38:32,757
and he shakes it in his hand

591
00:38:32,797 --> 00:38:35,891
and the narrator said, the Sahabah(صحابه) flew away.

592
00:38:36,736 --> 00:38:41,789
When Rasool Allah ﷺ shook the spear like flies would fly off the back of a camel,

593
00:38:42,602 --> 00:38:46,389
it was such a violent shaking of that spear.

594
00:38:46,897 --> 00:38:51,048
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ throws it at Obaey Bin Khalaf(أبيئ بن خلف),

595
00:38:51,468 --> 00:38:54,437
who was covered in armor, you can only see his eyes.

596
00:38:55,144 --> 00:39:00,419
But there was a small opening between the helmet and the armor on his neck.

597
00:39:01,218 --> 00:39:03,800
And the spear struck him right there.

598
00:39:04,685 --> 00:39:11,479
And it reached to his skin but it couldn't go through because of the steeled armor.

599
00:39:12,262 --> 00:39:14,993
But Obaey Bin Khalaf(أبيئ بن خلف) falls from his horse.

600
00:39:15,565 --> 00:39:20,601
And then he goes back running to his people bellowing like a bull, screaming.

601
00:39:21,238 --> 00:39:22,540
They told him What's wrong with you.

602
00:39:22,580 --> 00:39:23,782
He said: Muhammad(محمد) killed me.

603
00:39:24,082 --> 00:39:27,738
So, they uncovered him and they didn't see any injury in his neck,

604
00:39:28,035 --> 00:39:30,317
all what happened was some blood clotting

605
00:39:31,161 --> 00:39:33,703
because of the impact, but there was no injury.

606
00:39:33,743 --> 00:39:35,562
There was no bleeding, there was nothing.

607
00:39:35,947 --> 00:39:36,655
So, they told him;

608
00:39:36,695 --> 00:39:37,282
 لَا بَأسَ بِه

609
00:39:37,322 --> 00:39:38,189
there's nothing wrong with you.?

610
00:39:38,229 --> 00:39:39,469
Why are you so terrified?

611
00:39:39,817 --> 00:39:40,453
He said;

612
00:39:40,951 --> 00:39:43,816
Because Muhammad(محمد) told me that he will kill me,

613
00:39:43,886 --> 00:39:47,171
 so if he did nothing but spit on me, I would die.

614
00:39:47,581 --> 00:39:50,012
Subhan Allah(سبحان الله), they believe so much.

615
00:39:50,052 --> 00:39:54,113
They believed with certainty in anything that Rasool Allah ﷺ would say

616
00:39:55,017 --> 00:39:57,089
just because Rasool Allah ﷺ said, I will kill you.

617
00:39:57,319 --> 00:40:00,115
He believed that it would happen as Rasool Allah ﷺ said.

618
00:40:00,404 --> 00:40:02,605
In another narration, he said that

619
00:40:02,889 --> 00:40:08,881
if the pain I'm suffering is distributed among all of the people of Makkah, it would be sufficient to kill them.

620
00:40:09,291 --> 00:40:11,717
And very shortly after he died

621
00:40:12,733 --> 00:40:15,250
and this is a miracle of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

622
00:40:15,811 --> 00:40:20,869
because of the fact that he prophesized that he would kill Obaey Bin Khalaf(أبيئ بن خلف), and it happened.

623
00:40:21,369 --> 00:40:25,576
This is the only person whom we know for certain that Rasool Allah ﷺ killed.

624
00:40:25,945 --> 00:40:29,129
He could have killed many others in battles, but we don't know who they are.?

625
00:40:29,424 --> 00:40:32,146
He is the only one whose name is known.

626
00:40:32,614 --> 00:40:36,342
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says, and this is in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم).

627
00:40:36,641 --> 00:40:43,485
Great is Allah's wrath against the man, whom the messenger of Allah kills, in Allah's cause.

628
00:40:44,149 --> 00:40:48,724
The worst of men is the man on whom a messenger of Allah, any Messenger of Allah would kill.

629
00:40:49,552 --> 00:40:55,215
Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said, One night while he was traveling the same place  where Obaey Bin Khalaf(أبي بن خلف) was killed.

630
00:40:55,791 --> 00:40:58,001
He said suddenly I saw flames of fire.

631
00:40:58,469 --> 00:41:04,309
And then I saw a man being dragged in chains, asking for water

632
00:41:04,896 --> 00:41:09,234
and the response was don't provide him with any water.

633
00:41:09,605 --> 00:41:13,021
This is a man, who was killed by the Messenger of Allah.

634
00:41:13,547 --> 00:41:17,932
So, Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) was able to see the torment of Obaey Bin Khalaf(أبيئ بن خلف).

635
00:41:18,261 --> 00:41:28,055
And you see, it happens that some men would be able to see either punishment of kuffar(كفار)

636
00:41:28,471 --> 00:41:31,039
or the pleasure of Muslims

637
00:41:31,448 --> 00:41:35,624
that could happen in dreams or it could happen actually in front of you

638
00:41:35,815 --> 00:41:38,598
as what happened with Abdullah Bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) here.

639
00:41:39,549 --> 00:41:43,667
And what happened with the Aunt of Attaf Bin Khalid(عطاف بن خالد),

640
00:41:44,049 --> 00:41:46,636
who said that the Shuhadaa(شهدآء) responded to her Salaam(سلام),

641
00:41:47,388 --> 00:41:50,318
so that is something that is of Al-Ghaeb(ألغيب)

642
00:41:50,611 --> 00:41:54,835
but Allahعَزّوجَلّ brings it to the physical world even though it's in the other world,

643
00:41:54,875 --> 00:41:58,813
Allahعَزّوجَلّ reveals that sometimes to his servants.

644
00:42:00,065 --> 00:42:01,836
And we can consider these to be Karamaat(كرامات),

645
00:42:02,403 --> 00:42:06,560
both for this woman and for Abdullah Bin Umar رضي الله عنه.

646
00:42:07,565 --> 00:42:13,081
We'll talk about the role of women and it's important to talk about the role of women

647
00:42:13,648 --> 00:42:15,775
because we want our brothers to have role models

648
00:42:15,815 --> 00:42:19,432
and we also want our sisters to have role models from among As-Sahabiaat(ألصحابيات),

649
00:42:20,357 --> 00:42:22,230
since both brothers and sisters

650
00:42:23,129 --> 00:42:29,208
men and women are far away in their lifestyle from the way of the Sahabah(صحابه),

651
00:42:30,412 --> 00:42:35,165
you see because Islam was best understood by them.

652
00:42:36,327 --> 00:42:40,464
This was the best generation, therefore they are the closest to the truth

653
00:42:41,349 --> 00:42:43,562
and that makes their way the best way.

654
00:42:44,224 --> 00:42:46,066
So whenever you find that

655
00:42:46,339 --> 00:42:50,126
what you're doing is different or your understanding is different than that Sahabah(صحابه)

656
00:42:50,380 --> 00:42:54,663
realize that your way is the wrong way and there's was the right way.

657
00:42:55,984 --> 00:42:58,582
So let's take a look at the As-Sahabiaat(ألصحابيات) in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

658
00:42:59,466 --> 00:43:02,014
They used to provide water and medical assistance.

659
00:43:02,701 --> 00:43:03,972
Anas Ibn Malik(أنس ابن مالك) said;

660
00:43:04,343 --> 00:43:08,016
لَقَدْ رَاَيْتُ عَائشَه بِنْتِ اَبِيْ بَكْرْ وَ اُمُّ سَلِيْمْ

661
00:43:08,238 --> 00:43:15,380
وإنَّهُما لَمُشَمِّرَتَانِ، أَرَى خَدَمَ سُوقِهِن تَنْقُلَانِ القِرَبَ علَى مُتُونِهِمَا،

662
00:43:15,704 --> 00:43:19,998
 ثُمَّ تُفْرِغَانِهِ في أَفْوَاهِ القَوْمِ، ثُمَّ تَرْجِعَانِ فَتَمْلَآَنِهَا،

663
00:43:20,212 --> 00:43:22,974
 ثُمَّ تَجِيئَانِ فَتُفْرِغَانِهَا في أَفْوَاهِ القَوْمِ

664
00:43:23,216 --> 00:43:25,077
In Bukhari(بخاريْ), Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) said;

665
00:43:25,303 --> 00:43:29,763
I saw Ayesha Bint Abi Bakr(عائشه بنت ابي بكر) and Ummo Salim(ام سليم) tucken up their clothes.

666
00:43:29,828 --> 00:43:33,698
 And I could see their legs, their Shin, and this was before hijab

667
00:43:34,075 --> 00:43:38,419
and they were carrying buckets of water on their shoulders,

668
00:43:38,768 --> 00:43:43,228
and they would pour the water in the mouth of the soldiers.

669
00:43:43,835 --> 00:43:48,736
And then they would go back and fill them again and do the same, going back and forth.

670
00:43:49,502 --> 00:43:51,106
And you can also hear, see that

671
00:43:51,131 --> 00:43:52,282
Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله),

672
00:43:52,377 --> 00:43:54,027
Jihad(جهاد) for them was a family effort.

673
00:43:54,067 --> 00:43:57,777
I mean, the women participated in it, the men participated in it.

674
00:43:58,056 --> 00:44:00,349
Here you have Ayesha(عائشه), the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

675
00:44:00,389 --> 00:44:05,889
 the wife of the leader, is a servant, is serving the fighters.

676
00:44:05,992 --> 00:44:09,722
I mean, look at the leadership example that Rasool Allah ﷺ was giving.

677
00:44:10,232 --> 00:44:11,640
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said;

678
00:44:11,984 --> 00:44:15,486
رَاَيْتُ اُمُّ سَلِيْمْ بِنْت مَلْحَانُ و عَائشَه عَلَى ظُهْورِهِمَا الْقرَبْ

679
00:44:15,732 --> 00:44:20,431
يَحمِلَانَهُمَا يَوْمَ اُحَدْ وَكَانَت حمْنَهْ بِنْتِ جَحَشْ تسْىي الْعَطْشى وَتُداوي الجرحى

680
00:44:20,720 --> 00:44:22,632
وَكَانَتْ اُمْ اَيْمَنْ تَسْقِي الجَرْحَى

681
00:44:22,952 --> 00:44:27,400
Hamna Bint Jahash(حمنة بنت جحش) used to provide water to the thirsty

682
00:44:27,640 --> 00:44:31,949
 and she would give medical assistance to the injured

683
00:44:32,300 --> 00:44:35,544
and Umm Aiman(ام ايمن) used to provide water to the injured.

684
00:44:36,005 --> 00:44:37,430
Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) would say,

685
00:44:37,465 --> 00:44:42,307
كَانَ رَسٌول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يَغْزُوْ بِاُمِّ سَلِيْمْ وَنِسْوَة وَمِنَّ الْاَنْصَارِ مَعَه’ اِذَا غَزَا

686
00:44:42,577 --> 00:44:44,829
 فَيَسْقِيْنَ مَاءَ وَيُدَاوِيْنَ الْجَرْحَى

687
00:44:44,853 --> 00:44:47,085
And this is in Muslim(المسلم), Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) said;

688
00:44:47,156 --> 00:44:50,818
When Rasool Allah ﷺ would go out to fight in battle.

689
00:44:50,949 --> 00:44:54,250
He would take with him Umm-O-Salim(ام سليم), and some woman from Al-Ansaar(الانصار)

690
00:44:54,535 --> 00:44:55,649
to serve the army.

691
00:44:56,157 --> 00:45:00,965
And this shows you that women would accompany the armies of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

692
00:45:01,663 --> 00:45:03,481
In the time of Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب)

693
00:45:03,957 --> 00:45:10,862
he received pieces of cloth, so he was handing them out to the women of Madina.

694
00:45:11,212 --> 00:45:16,811
So, this nice cloth remains and some of the ones who are there said,

695
00:45:17,184 --> 00:45:21,708
O Ameer Ul Momineen(امير المؤمنين) give this to the daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

696
00:45:22,070 --> 00:45:25,034
your wife and they're referring to the daughter of Ali(علي).

697
00:45:25,402 --> 00:45:29,565
They call her the daughter of Rasool Ullah because she's the granddaughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

698
00:45:29,605 --> 00:45:31,957
 she's Umm Kalsoom Bint Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب).

699
00:45:32,496 --> 00:45:33,849
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: No.

700
00:45:34,721 --> 00:45:36,847
Umm-O-Salim(ام سليم) deserves it more.

701
00:45:37,255 --> 00:45:40,823
She was one of the women of Al-Ansaar(الانصار), who gave Baiyah(بيعة) to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

702
00:45:41,169 --> 00:45:45,610
and she was the one giving us water on the day of Uhud(أحَد).

703
00:45:46,023 --> 00:45:52,636
So, Umar رضي الله عنه was recognizing the effort of this woman years later.

704
00:45:53,560 --> 00:45:54,802
He's talking about Umm-O-Salim(ام سليم)

705
00:45:54,882 --> 00:46:02,968
 and in this affair, it was the women of Al-Ansaar(الانصار), who deserve special recognition for their effort.

706
00:46:03,335 --> 00:46:06,814
And again, as I said, you'll hear me say again and again

707
00:46:06,854 --> 00:46:10,181
this is what it means to carry the title of Ansaari(انصاري).

708
00:46:10,998 --> 00:46:15,571
Even their woman would give everything for the service of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

709
00:46:16,104 --> 00:46:17,354
Fatima(فاطمه) also participated.

710
00:46:17,394 --> 00:46:20,941
Al-Bukhari(البخاري) said: Fatima(فاطمه) washed him, referring to Rasool Allah ﷺ

711
00:46:20,981 --> 00:46:23,293
and Ali(علي) poured the water from a shield.

712
00:46:23,893 --> 00:46:27,356
And when Fatima(فاطمه) saw that the water was only increasing the blood flow

713
00:46:27,694 --> 00:46:30,697
she took a piece of matting and set fire to it,

714
00:46:30,795 --> 00:46:34,504
then attached it to the wound and the blood seized flowing.

715
00:46:34,840 --> 00:46:38,608
We talked about that earlier, when we talked about the injury of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

716
00:46:39,622 --> 00:46:44,828
Not only did the woman act in supporting roles for the army,

717
00:46:45,356 --> 00:46:49,908
like taking care of the injured and delivering water to the soldiers

718
00:46:50,358 --> 00:46:54,793
but there are also incidents where women fought with the sword.

719
00:46:55,520 --> 00:46:59,508
 And the example of that would be in Musaibah Bint Ka'ab رضي الله عنها

720
00:47:00,294 --> 00:47:01,379
this was a strong woman

721
00:47:02,165 --> 00:47:05,149
And in Uhud(أحَد) she fought with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

722
00:47:05,816 --> 00:47:08,322
And she fought in more than one battle.

723
00:47:08,362 --> 00:47:14,031
And she even fought in the time of Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه against Musailimah Al-Kazzaab(مسيلمه الكذاب).

724
00:47:14,535 --> 00:47:20,820
And when she died her granddaughter said I was one of those who washed her

725
00:47:21,123 --> 00:47:23,579
and she had 13 injuries in her body.

726
00:47:23,967 --> 00:47:25,903
And the worst of them was the one,

727
00:47:26,125 --> 00:47:29,596
the scar left behind because of the sword of Ibn Qamiyah(ابن قمعة)

728
00:47:29,636 --> 00:47:33,697
Ibn Qamiyah(ابن قمعه), the one who injured Rasool Allah ﷺ, struck her on her shoulder

729
00:47:34,099 --> 00:47:36,872
when she stood in front of Rasool Allah ﷺ to defend him,

730
00:47:37,640 --> 00:47:39,856
and that was the worst of the scars.

731
00:47:40,253 --> 00:47:42,805
And she would suffer other scars in other battles.

732
00:47:43,199 --> 00:47:48,567
And for example, we talked about this in the series on Abu Bakr Siddique رضي الله عنه,

733
00:47:48,834 --> 00:47:52,227
that she suffered injuries in the battle against Musailimah Al-Kazzaab(مسيلمه الكذاب)

734
00:47:52,775 --> 00:47:59,023
and the way those injuries were healed was by pouring boiling oil over them.

735
00:47:59,511 --> 00:48:06,891
And she said that the process of healing was worse and more painful than the injuries themselves.

736
00:48:07,327 --> 00:48:11,867
 And for example, this injury here that she suffered from Ibn Qamiyah(ابن قميه) in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

737
00:48:12,282 --> 00:48:16,628
For one year, she was suffering the pain from that injury.

738
00:48:16,708 --> 00:48:18,161
It took one year to heal.

739
00:48:18,760 --> 00:48:20,004
That was how bad it was,

740
00:48:20,424 --> 00:48:24,249
and Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) even though she suffered, Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) how many injuries on the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

741
00:48:24,814 --> 00:48:29,254
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was going out to Hamrah Al-Asad(حمراء الاسد), the next day, she wanted to go out.

742
00:48:29,763 --> 00:48:32,774
But when she stood up, she collapsed, she couldn't go any further.

743
00:48:33,842 --> 00:48:37,434
This is how strong the drive in her spirit was.

744
00:48:37,695 --> 00:48:39,838
May Allah be pleased with her.

745
00:48:40,444 --> 00:48:43,963
When Rasool Allah ﷺ went to Hamrah Al-Asad(حمراء الاسد), immediately when he came back

746
00:48:44,300 --> 00:48:46,747
he sent someone to ask about her

747
00:48:47,187 --> 00:48:50,260
and they came back to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said she's getting better.

748
00:48:50,300 --> 00:48:51,651
And Rasool Allah ﷺ was very happy.

749
00:48:52,140 --> 00:48:58,651
And this also shows you another dimension of Rasool Allah ﷺ he cared for the Sahabah(صحابه),

750
00:48:59,162 --> 00:49:03,124
he would ask about them, he wanted to know how well they were doing.

751
00:49:03,616 --> 00:49:06,819
They were on his mind, they were on his mind, he would think about them,

752
00:49:07,239 --> 00:49:09,136
and this is how the leader should be.

753
00:49:09,898 --> 00:49:14,756
Examples of the patience of these Sahabiaat رضي الله عنهن.

754
00:49:15,030 --> 00:49:17,748
Saffiyyah(صفيه) we mentioned part of what happened to her.

755
00:49:17,962 --> 00:49:20,121
 Saffiyyah(صفيه) was the sister of Hamzah(حمزه)

756
00:49:20,560 --> 00:49:24,086
and when she received the news that Hamza(حمزه) was killed

757
00:49:24,292 --> 00:49:26,705
 she wanted to go and take a look at his body

758
00:49:27,242 --> 00:49:31,518
and we mentioned that when Rasool Allah ﷺ saw her, he told Az-Zubair(الزبير) to go and stop her.

759
00:49:32,462 --> 00:49:36,548
So, Az-Zubair(الزبير) stops her and she pushes him aside and said;

760
00:49:37,432 --> 00:49:46,852
بلغني أنه مثل بأخي وذلك في الله فما أرضانا بما كان من ذلك لأحتسبن و لأصبرن إن شاء الله

761
00:49:47,351 --> 00:49:48,420
Why are you stopping me?

762
00:49:49,147 --> 00:49:51,903
I have been told how my brother has been mutilated

763
00:49:52,666 --> 00:49:54,135
That was in Allah's cause.

764
00:49:54,702 --> 00:49:57,093
And that fact has comforted us

765
00:49:57,549 --> 00:50:01,740
I will keep myself under control and remain calm if Allah wills it

766
00:50:01,780 --> 00:50:03,310
 and he was mutilated badly.

767
00:50:03,350 --> 00:50:09,366
 I mean, they cut his nose, his ears, his private parts, they opened up his stomach and chest.

768
00:50:09,930 --> 00:50:12,977
 So he was badly disfigured.

769
00:50:14,152 --> 00:50:18,709
But she insisted on seeing him and Rasool Allah ﷺ let her see him.

770
00:50:19,473 --> 00:50:24,061
And she went and stood over the body of Hamza رضي الله عنه.

771
00:50:24,886 --> 00:50:26,456
Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) said; she looked at him,

772
00:50:27,579 --> 00:50:28,982
She said a prayer over him,

773
00:50:29,511 --> 00:50:31,006
asked forgiveness for him,

774
00:50:31,616 --> 00:50:36,734
and then spoke the words to Allah we belong and to Him do we return.

775
00:50:37,303 --> 00:50:39,803
إِنَّا لِلّهِ وَإِنَّـا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعونَ

776
00:50:41,188 --> 00:50:45,895
This is how, we should dealt with the calamity of losing your brother and seeing him in that condition

777
00:50:46,592 --> 00:50:48,887
 إِنَّا لِلّهِ وَإِنَّـا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعونَ

778
00:50:49,434 --> 00:50:52,497
I want you to take a moment and think about the meanings of these words.

779
00:50:52,725 --> 00:50:55,125
This is what we say when a disaster befalls us

780
00:50:55,610 --> 00:50:56,723
إِنَّا لِلّهِ

781
00:50:56,922 --> 00:50:58,035
We belong to Allah.

782
00:50:58,782 --> 00:51:00,830
Meaning if I lost a loved one

783
00:51:01,294 --> 00:51:02,883
that loved one belongs to Allah.

784
00:51:03,546 --> 00:51:07,227
And if I think that anything belongs to me, in Duniyah(دنيا), No

785
00:51:08,152 --> 00:51:12,413
me and my belongings belong to Allahعَزّوجَلّ if that's the case,

786
00:51:13,140 --> 00:51:15,454
then it is the property owner,

787
00:51:15,825 --> 00:51:19,661
who has the right to call in, his property and claim it whenever he wants.

788
00:51:20,677 --> 00:51:22,451
If Hamza(حمزه) belongs to Allah,

789
00:51:22,978 --> 00:51:26,049
then Allah is the One, Who has the right to call him in, whenever He wants.

790
00:51:27,450 --> 00:51:29,776
This is very important for the Muslim to realize that

791
00:51:30,272 --> 00:51:31,871
I might have wealth in my hand now.

792
00:51:31,911 --> 00:51:34,141
I might have a family whom I consider to be my family.

793
00:51:34,181 --> 00:51:37,884
 But in reality, all of this property of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

794
00:51:38,590 --> 00:51:39,217
And then;

795
00:51:39,415 --> 00:51:40,479
 وَإِنَّـا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعونَ

796
00:51:40,519 --> 00:51:41,582
And we're going to go back to Him.

797
00:51:41,622 --> 00:51:43,897
Eventually, we're going to go back to Him.

798
00:51:43,952 --> 00:51:47,905
 So, I shouldn't be so upset, if I lose something now

799
00:51:47,945 --> 00:51:50,460
because eventually everything is going to go back to Him.

800
00:51:50,997 --> 00:51:52,179
So, it's gonna happen,

801
00:51:52,497 --> 00:51:57,504
regardless it shouldn't make much of a difference if it happens today or tomorrow.

802
00:51:58,487 --> 00:52:01,213
Another example Hamna Bin Jahash(حمنه بنت جحش).

803
00:52:01,924 --> 00:52:05,172
Hamna Bin Jahash(حمنه بنت جحش) is the sister of Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش).

804
00:52:05,707 --> 00:52:12,007
And we talked about what happened to Abdullah Bin Jahash رضي الله عنه

805
00:52:12,654 --> 00:52:16,652
and her father also died and her husband Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب ابن عمير) died.

806
00:52:16,851 --> 00:52:19,663
So, she lost the three closest men to her.

807
00:52:20,647 --> 00:52:23,266
She came to meet the army

808
00:52:23,334 --> 00:52:29,167
I mean she was there with the army as we said that she was delivering water to them

809
00:52:29,207 --> 00:52:30,908
 but when the news was brought to her,

810
00:52:31,535 --> 00:52:34,695
they told her, your father has passed away.

811
00:52:35,694 --> 00:52:36,044
She said;

812
00:52:36,084 --> 00:52:37,885
 إِنَّا لِلّهِ وَإِنَّـا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعونَ

813
00:52:38,218 --> 00:52:39,385
She was composed.

814
00:52:40,089 --> 00:52:43,346
They told her, Your brother Abdullah(عبدالله) has died

815
00:52:44,064 --> 00:52:45,870
And she was also calm and she said;

816
00:52:45,910 --> 00:52:47,540
إِنَّا لِلّهِ وَإِنَّـا إِلَيْهِ رَاجِعونَ

817
00:52:47,580 --> 00:52:48,317
Patient,

818
00:52:49,134 --> 00:52:53,242
and then they said, And your husband Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب ابن عمير) died

819
00:52:53,565 --> 00:52:55,271
 and then she screamed.

820
00:52:56,014 --> 00:52:58,032
When Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that he said?

821
00:52:58,749 --> 00:53:01,979
A woman's husband has a very special place with her.

822
00:53:02,764 --> 00:53:04,115
That's the narration of Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق),

823
00:53:04,155 --> 00:53:06,389
 and in the narration of Ibn Majah(ابن ماجه),

824
00:53:06,429 --> 00:53:12,939
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: A husband alone, has control over part of his wife's feelings.

825
00:53:13,311 --> 00:53:15,414
So, the husband is special to his wife.

826
00:53:16,126 --> 00:53:20,310
And she was composed when, she heard the news of her father and brother.

827
00:53:20,883 --> 00:53:24,333
But when she heard the news of her husband, that was too much and then she broke down,

828
00:53:25,015 --> 00:53:26,683
when they asked her, why.?

829
00:53:26,723 --> 00:53:27,433
 She said;

830
00:53:27,668 --> 00:53:30,724
That is because I remember that my children will be orphaned.

831
00:53:31,514 --> 00:53:35,377
Rasool Allah ﷺ made Dua(دعا) for her.

832
00:53:36,091 --> 00:53:38,084
Another example is a Dinariya(ديناريه).

833
00:53:38,842 --> 00:53:42,290
She lost her husband, brother and father.

834
00:53:43,244 --> 00:53:47,487
They came to her and said your husband, brother and father were killed.

835
00:53:48,218 --> 00:53:51,280
She said and how is the Messenger of Allah?

836
00:53:52,314 --> 00:53:56,250
they said; he is fine, he's just as you might wish.

837
00:53:56,783 --> 00:53:58,432
She said show him to me.

838
00:53:58,789 --> 00:53:59,845
I want to see him.

839
00:54:00,532 --> 00:54:08,068
 And when Rasool Allah ﷺ was pointed out to her, she said every loss other than you is trivial.

840
00:54:08,497 --> 00:54:11,645
It doesn't matter what I lose, whatever I lose is trivial.

841
00:54:12,118 --> 00:54:14,139
As long as, you are fine.

842
00:54:14,972 --> 00:54:16,915
And dear brothers and sisters,

843
00:54:17,898 --> 00:54:23,417
We talked a lot about loving Rasool Allah ﷺ, we talked a lot about sacrifice,

844
00:54:24,347 --> 00:54:28,947
and you see these will remain intangible theoretical concepts

845
00:54:30,300 --> 00:54:33,376
until we see how the Sahabah(صحابه) lived them.

846
00:54:34,050 --> 00:54:37,756
If you want to know what it means to take a look at this woman.

847
00:54:38,926 --> 00:54:43,316
She receives the news of the death of her husband, father and brother

848
00:54:43,765 --> 00:54:48,215
and she only thinks about Rasool Allah ﷺ, how is he.?

849
00:54:48,742 --> 00:54:50,115
And when she knows that he's alive.

850
00:54:50,155 --> 00:54:56,306
She wants to see him, she wants to satisfy her eyes with getting a glimpse of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

851
00:54:57,130 --> 00:55:01,322
And then she says everything, everything is trivial,

852
00:55:01,701 --> 00:55:02,961
as long as you are fine.

853
00:55:04,085 --> 00:55:06,258
This is what it means to love Rasool Allah ﷺ.

854
00:55:08,330 --> 00:55:11,580
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to make us of those who love Him

855
00:55:12,310 --> 00:55:13,591
and to love His messenger

856
00:55:14,396 --> 00:55:17,783
and to love the Sahabah(صحابه) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

857
00:55:18,642 --> 00:55:22,719
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

858
00:55:22,948 --> 00:55:25,487
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

